 "response": "**Kakir's budget is now $1075K.**\n\nHow I got there:\n\n- **Which records count:** Only Finance Office budget entries count. The PMO, Sales, Legal, Engineering, Vendor, Facilities, Operations and Marketing messages do not change the budget. Finance Office entries that are not budget figures (audits, purchase orders, receipts, reminders) also have no effect.\n- **Withdrawal chains:** For each chain I started from the last withdrawal and worked back. A withdrawal counts only if nothing later withdraws it. Some examples:\n  - **#0003 still applies.** Its withdrawal #0007 was cancelled by #0111. The chain continues through #0711, #0956, #1023 and #1039, and ends with #0111 in effect.\n  - **#0005 is removed.** Its withdrawal #0008 stays in effect because #0073, which would have cancelled it, was itself withdrawn by #0414.\n  - **#0066 is removed.** #1263 stays in effect because #1470, which would have cancelled it, was withdrawn by #1533.\n  - About 140 budget updates end up withdrawn. These include #0017, #0030, #0176, #0198, #0261, #0463, #0539, #0852 and #1337.\n- **Calculation:** I started from the $1280K set by #0001. I then applied each remaining budget increase or decrease once, in record order. The running total after the last effective entry (#1599, \u2212$75K) is $1075K.\n\nI did not run a separate second pass to check the total.\n\nANSWER: $1075K",
